    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d357">

                <pb facs="0439" n="267" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg267"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/4084</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Haiti</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bailly-Blanchard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-04-26T15:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 26, 1917, 3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 6 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Pursuant to cable received from Minister Ménos stating that Department promised
                    Haiti <hi rendition="#italic">appui convertible</hi>, Minister for Foreign <pb
                        facs="0440" n="268" xml:id="pg268"/> Affairs called to ask this Legation to
                    ascertain precisely what support the United States would give to Haiti in the
                    event of her declaring war against the Imperial German Government. Respectfully
                    urge early reply.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Blanchard</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
